sxml encode - Write an XML document as an EXI stream

Usage: sxml encode [--alignment=ALIGNMENT] [--preserve=LIST] [--fragment] [--strict] [--self-contained] [--block-size=N] [--value-max-length=N] [--value-partition-capacity=N] [--schema=FILE] [--include-cookie] [--include-options] [--include-schema-id] [--canonical] [--omit-options-document] [--utc-time] [--self-contained-element=NAME]... [--output=FILE] [--force] INPUT

Parses INPUT as XML and writes it as an EXI 1.0 stream (Efficient XML
Interchange) to standard output: bytes, with no line feed after them.

The EXI options say what the stream keeps and how it is laid out:
--alignment=bit-packed (the default), byte-alignment, pre-compression
or compression (DEFLATE); --preserve=LIST, a comma-separated list of
comments, pis, dtd, prefixes and lexical-values (none by default);
--fragment for a stream of elements with no document around them;
--strict; --block-size=N, --value-max-length=N and
--value-partition-capacity=N. --schema=FILE encodes with the
schema-informed grammars of the XSD in FILE.

A decoder needs the options the stream was written with: give it the
same flags, or write them into the stream's header with
--include-options (and the schemaId with --include-schema-id).
--include-cookie begins the stream with "$EXI".

--canonical writes Canonical EXI, one stream for one document and one
set of options; --omit-options-document leaves its options document
out of the header, --utc-time writes its date-times in UTC.
--self-contained-element=NAME (repeatable, with --self-contained)
writes each element NAME so that it can be read on its own.

--output=FILE (-o FILE) writes the stream to FILE instead, and only
when the command succeeds; a FILE that exists is replaced only with
--force.

Exit status: 0 on success, 1 when INPUT is not well-formed or the
options cannot represent it, 2 for a bad option value, 3 when a file
cannot be read or written.

Options:
  -h, --help                         Show this help and exit
      --alignment=ALIGNMENT          EXI alignment of the stream (one of: bit-packed, byte-alignment, pre-compression, compression; default: bit-packed)
      --preserve=LIST                EXI fidelity: comments,pis,dtd,prefixes,lexical-values
      --fragment                     The EXI stream is a fragment, not a document
      --strict                       Strict schema-informed EXI grammars
      --self-contained               The EXI stream may hold self-contained elements
      --block-size=N                 EXI values per compression block
      --value-max-length=N           Longest EXI value kept in the string table
      --value-partition-capacity=N   Most EXI values in the string table
      --schema=FILE                  XSD of the stream's schema-informed grammars
      --include-cookie               Begin the stream with the EXI cookie $EXI
      --include-options              Write the EXI options into the stream's header
      --include-schema-id            Write the schemaId into the header's options
      --canonical                    Write Canonical EXI
      --omit-options-document        Canonical EXI without the options document in the header
      --utc-time                     Canonical EXI with date-times in UTC
      --self-contained-element=NAME  An element to write self-contained, NCName or Q{uri}local (with --self-contained) (repeatable)
  -o, --output=FILE                  Write the result to FILE instead of standard output
      --force                        Replace files that exist instead of refusing

Arguments:
  INPUT  XML document to encode; - reads standard input

Examples:
  sxml encode --output=orders.exi orders.xml
  sxml encode --alignment=compression --preserve=comments,prefixes --output=orders.exi orders.xml
  sxml encode --include-options orders.xml | sxml decode -
